* Callers for the submarine (openc2e Creatures 2 project, our own script;
* the game's own caller picture). Run by openc2e after the world loads
* (Additions folder); made anew each load.
*
* The submarine (vehicle 3 1 2) had no callers: it moved only by its own two
* arrow buttons, each a fixed leg from each stop (owner, 2026-11-19, night:
* "add the style of caller ... and I would like that to call the submarine
* from its current stopped position"; then "make three"). Its stops are its
* OV00: 0 the west dock (in the sea cave under the stalactites), 1 the
* airlock (the tunnel under the seabed), 2 the east dock. Its activate 1
* goes on round the loop (0 to 1, 1 to 2, 2 to 0) and activate 2 back the
* other way (0 to 2, 2 to 1, 1 to 0), so every stop is one leg from every
* other. It is taken to be docked when it is still and at the dock its OV00
* names (west: left x under 6120, top above 850; airlock: left x 6400-6520,
* top below 1200; east: left x over 7100, top above 860).
*
* Its scripts clear its ATTR 4 (activateable) while it travels and set it
* again when it docks; Home's submarine was docked at the airlock with ATTR
* 8, without it (a save mid-trip, likely), so its own arrows did nothing and
* the next trip's "subv attr 4" would have cleared another bit. A
* submarine found still at its dock without it gets it back at load.
*
* A caller at each stop (2 2 223 west, 224 airlock, 225 east; the game's
* capsule caller picture, lbtn, as the lifts' callers; OV01 its stop): a
* press, by the hand or a creature, brings the submarine to its stop from
* wherever it is docked, by the one leg that goes there; while it is
* travelling, or already there, nothing happens.
*   west    x 6280, on the sea-cave walkway's floor (y 892), on the cave wall
*           right of the docked submarine (the owner's spot)
*   airlock x 6416, in the chamber between its west door and the docked
*           submarine, on the floor (about 1446)
*   east    x 7386, on the dock's floor (906), right of the docked submarine
enum 3 1 2
  doif velx eq 0 and vely eq 0
    setv var1 attr andv var1 4
    doif var1 eq 0 addv attr 4 endi
  endi
next
enum 2 2 223 kill targ next
enum 2 2 224 kill targ next
enum 2 2 225 kill targ next
inst new: simp lbtn 6 0 5000 0 setv cls2 2 2 223 setv attr 4 bhvr 1 0 pose 0 setv ov01 0 mvto 6280 812 slow
inst new: simp lbtn 6 0 5000 0 setv cls2 2 2 224 setv attr 4 bhvr 1 0 pose 0 setv ov01 1 mvto 6416 1366 slow
inst new: simp lbtn 6 0 5000 0 setv cls2 2 2 225 setv attr 4 bhvr 1 0 pose 0 setv ov01 2 mvto 7386 826 slow

scrp 2 2 223 1
  pose 5 snde but2
  setv var0 ov01
  enum 3 1 2
    setv var3 -1
    doif velx eq 0 and vely eq 0
      doif posl lt 6120 and post lt 850 setv var3 0 endi
      doif posl gt 6400 and posl lt 6520 and post gt 1200 setv var3 1 endi
      doif posl gt 7100 and post lt 860 setv var3 2 endi
    endi
    doif var3 eq ov00 and ov00 ne var0
      setv var2 ov00 addv var2 1 modv var2 3
      doif var2 eq var0
        mesg writ targ 0
      else
        mesg writ targ 1
      endi
    endi
  next
  wait 20 pose 0 setv actv 0
endm
scrp 2 2 223 2
  mesg writ ownr 0
  setv actv 0
endm
scrp 2 2 223 0
  setv var0 0
endm

scrp 2 2 224 1
  pose 5 snde but2
  setv var0 ov01
  enum 3 1 2
    setv var3 -1
    doif velx eq 0 and vely eq 0
      doif posl lt 6120 and post lt 850 setv var3 0 endi
      doif posl gt 6400 and posl lt 6520 and post gt 1200 setv var3 1 endi
      doif posl gt 7100 and post lt 860 setv var3 2 endi
    endi
    doif var3 eq ov00 and ov00 ne var0
      setv var2 ov00 addv var2 1 modv var2 3
      doif var2 eq var0
        mesg writ targ 0
      else
        mesg writ targ 1
      endi
    endi
  next
  wait 20 pose 0 setv actv 0
endm
scrp 2 2 224 2
  mesg writ ownr 0
  setv actv 0
endm
scrp 2 2 224 0
  setv var0 0
endm

